          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em fibre bundle
            or
            %em fiber bundle
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            in which every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibre"} fibre
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            %em standard fibre
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em typical fiber
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial"} locally trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            with that typical fiber.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            In the most general sense, a
            %strong bundle
            over an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: E \to B
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            In appropriate contexts, a
            %strong fibre bundle
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            with standard fibre
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            may be defined as a bundle over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            such that, given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: 1 \to B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is isomorphic to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            which is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separator
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointed category
          %p
            One often writes a typical fibre bundle in shorthand as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to E \to B
            or
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {
                  F &amp; \rightarrow &amp; E \\
                  \&amp;             &amp; \downarrow \\
                  \&amp;             &amp; B
                  }
          %p
            even though there is not a single morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to E
            but instead one for each global element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            (and none at all if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            has no global elements!).
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial"} locally
