          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %h3#in_higher_category_theory In higher category theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            the notion of fiber bundle generalizes. See
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"}> associated ∞-bundle
              \.
          %h3#in_commutative_algebra In commutative algebra
          %p
            Under the interpretation of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/module#RelationToVectorBundlesInIntroduction"} modules as generalized vector bundles
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+free+modules"} locally free modules
          %h3#in_noncommutative_geometry In noncommutative geometry
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
            both principal and associated bundles have analogues. The principal bundles over noncommutative spaces typically have structure group replaced by a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf--Galois+extensions"} Hopf–Galois extensions
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToFibrations Relation to fibrations
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial"} locally trivial
              topological fiber bundle projection is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibration"} Hurewicz fibration
              if it is also a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/numerable+bundle"} numerable bundle
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              out of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+triviality"} local triviality
              and the local recognition of Serre fibrations (
              %a{:href => "Serre+fibration#MapIsSerreFibrationIfLocallySo"}> this Prop
              ) and of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibrations"} Hurewicz fibrations
              (
              %a{:href => "Hurewicz+fibration#MapIsHurewiczFibrationIfPullbackToNumerableCoverIsSo"}> this Prop.
              ), respectively.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p Beware that the converse statement is far from being true.
